<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <RootNamespace>AddedObjectRemover</RootNamespace>
    <Description>The rules of objects resting on removed ones and of other mods' objects left without support: support contacts and weights, touch chains, the resting and touch rules, the also-remove rounds that repeat until nothing more goes, the drop test and landing, the support world, the held-up targets and the holders of objects that stay, the keep, remove or pull-down decision for other mods' objects and its rounds, and the report-file details that read the rounds' internals. It references its contracts, CollectPlacedObjects.Contracts, RemovalDecisionList.Contracts and IdentifyTheMods.Contracts (the placed objects, decisions and trust it judges with), FindTargetObjectsToKeep.Contracts (the held-up targets it finds), BaseObjectShapeAndKind.Contracts and RunCaches.Contracts (the shapes, triangles, surface samples and terrain it measures), Ids, PluginRecordFacts and the package-free tools it uses, and holds no packages.</Description>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\ObjectsRestingOnRemovedOnes.Contracts\ObjectsRestingOnRemovedOnes.Contracts.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Steps\CollectPlacedObjects.Contracts\CollectPlacedObjects.Contracts.csproj" />
